      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}\n\nAll together because of the Edits i did Later.\n\nThe problem itself is on all Persons Physbones and not only me.\n\nThis is a Created Test Avatar with Physbones that has stretch. (Added a Toggle To Switch between 2 Physbone Scipts one with Stretch and one without any stretch)\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_2a973e01-105e-479b-b266-5206b3e01afb \n\n(https://youtu.be/RjYOLwbB1lA) - Its like this Avatar without the Extras but with GoLoco because its good for testing. (Stats are in the Screenshot)\n\nThe Jitter or Lag or Snapping or what ever it category it get puts in Started with the Beta 1511 and with 1517 some exeptions was fixed both other where more noticable.\n\nAll Physbones are Directly set to the bone and are not connected or attached with Constraints.\n\n \n\nHere the Videos i Made over time that showes a bit of the Problem.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/kRAB0dpbCGE (Change between 1517 and 1507)\n\nhttps://youtu.be/_SSoe3NsOCs (2 Avatars with 1517 and its more noticable with the Second Avatar)\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KkrJQjArlLE (First test with Live 1518\n\n in 3rd person view)\n\n--------\n\nWhat i have tested:\n\nInstalling Older Drives.\n\nReinstall VRChat on another Drive and removed any config related stuff.\n\nChanged the FPS setting and any other related setting.\n\nIts in VR(Half Body) and Desktop but VR is in the Current state not playable for me because it gives me very fast nausea\n\n--------",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
